1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,156
What should you send your accountant

2
00:00:02,156 --> 00:00:02,759
at tax time?

3
00:00:03,059 --> 00:00:04,887
Not a shoebox. Four things.

4
00:00:05,337 --> 00:00:06,535
One. The period.

5
00:00:06,535 --> 00:00:08,475
The exact dates your records cover.

6
00:00:08,775 --> 00:00:11,660
Two. The receipts themselves, readable.

7
00:00:11,660 --> 00:00:12,964
Photos, emails, PDFs.

8
00:00:13,264 --> 00:00:14,820
Three. A summary you’ve checked.

9
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:16,399
Date, store and amount.

10
00:00:16,699 --> 00:00:18,343
Four. A short list of anything

11
00:00:18,343 --> 00:00:19,980
you couldn’t find or explain.

12
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:21,144
Instead of guessing.

13
00:00:21,594 --> 00:00:22,620
Why it matters:

14
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:24,165
you’re paying for their time.

15
00:00:24,165 --> 00:00:25,936
Every receipt they have to decode

16
00:00:25,936 --> 00:00:27,131
is time on your bill.

17
00:00:27,581 --> 00:00:28,665
And ask first.

18
00:00:28,665 --> 00:00:30,831
Many accountants have a format they prefer.

19
00:00:31,331 --> 00:00:33,285
Find us at receipt-nest.com,

20
00:00:33,285 --> 00:00:35,030
on the App Store and Google Play.
